00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:18.000
Every afternoon, Thomas the Tank Engine puffs along his branch line with Annie and Clarabel.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.490
First, they pass the Waterloo.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:25.290
Next, they come to a big farm.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:30.000
Then, they can see a bridge with a village nestled either side of it.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:37.100
this is a special place. Whenever children hear Thomas coming along, they stand on the

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:45.620
bridge waving until he is out of sight. One day, Thomas was running late. He had stopped

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:52.210
at the signal before the bridge to talk to some new children. Percy was waiting too.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:58.080
"Hurry up, Thomas," called Percy when the signal dropped. "If you're late, the Fat Controller

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.000
may get a new engine to replace you."

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:09.430
you? He would never do that, thought Thomas, but he was worried. Next day, Thomas hurried

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:17.130
along the line. Just ahead was a good job. There, on the platform, was an inspector waving

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:27.230
a red flag. Next, Thomas saw some children. They were waving too. Something must be wrong,

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.000
thought Thomas. This station is for goods.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:36.490
not passengers help Thomas help we are glad to see you call the children please

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:42.480
will you take us home the station master explained to Thomas's driver that the

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:46.760
school bus had broken down and that all the parents would be worried if the

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:53.100
children were late Thomas waited as the children walked down from the bridge then

00:12:53.100 --> 00:13:00.000
he took them to the next station where Bertie was waiting to take them home

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.330
When Thomas finished his journey, he was very late.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:07.830
He was worried that the Fat Controller might be cross with him.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.770
I warned, Thomas, puffed Percy to James.

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:16.250
He's been late one time too many. He'll be in trouble now.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:25.960
But next morning, the Fat Controller was nowhere to be seen.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:40.040
"Thank goodness," sighed Thomas.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.750
Thomas knows every part of his branch line,

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:50.890
but just ahead was a stretch where the hot sun had bent the rails on the track.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:57.620
"Careful, Thomas," called his driver, but it was too late.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:05.470
"That's done it," said his driver. "We shan't get any further today."

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.910
"But what about my passengers?"

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:12.610
"Don't worry, they'll be looked after," replied his driver.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:19.880
While Workman repaired the line, Thomas had to shunt trucks in the yard.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:24.930
Bertie came to see him. "I understand you need my help again."

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:29.760
"Yes, Bertie," replied Thomas sadly. "I can't run without my rails."

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:40.860
Bertie set off to collect Thomas's passengers. "Hello Bertie," they said. "We are glad you are here."

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:50.390
Bertie drove along the road by the railway. He stopped at each station along the line.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:56.450
Sometimes he stopped between stations to let people off closer to their homes.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.000
Thomas felt miserable. "I've lost

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:06.300
my passengers. They like Bertie better than me." The Fat Controller arrived. "Your branch

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:11.520
line is repaired. I'm going to change your timetable so that you and Bertie can work

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:20.390
together more." When Thomas reached the station, there were all his passengers. "Bertie is

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:24.250
a very good boss, but we missed our train rides with you," they said.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:29.570
Later, Thomas spoke to Bertie. "Thank you for looking after my passengers."

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:35.040
That's all right, Thomas. I like to make new friends, but I'm glad to share them with you.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:39.440
Bertie, said Thomas, you're a very good friend indeed.

