02:51:20.430 --> 02:51:24.790
And where there are lots of people, there is food, as every cat knows.

02:51:25.470 --> 02:51:30.000
Henry's cat went in, and soon found a snack bar, and after a pickled onion milk

02:51:30.000 --> 02:51:33.300
and a marzipan sandwich felt much better.

02:51:33.300 --> 02:51:35.900
So he thought he would walk around the exhibition.

02:51:35.900 --> 02:51:39.030
It was all about computers and robots.

02:51:39.030 --> 02:51:44.600
Now even the cleverest cats don't know much about robots and computers

02:51:44.600 --> 02:51:50.540
as they are not tasty, smelly, chasey, or warm.

02:51:50.540 --> 02:51:54.350
So there's not much point in knowing about them.

02:51:54.350 --> 02:51:56.760
Henry's cat looked around to see what was going on.

02:51:56.760 --> 02:51:59.320
There were computers that could walk,

02:52:00.730 --> 02:52:10.470
Or I am a computer drawer, tell the time, just traffic wardens and even cook.

02:52:11.520 --> 02:52:17.060
There was even a lecturer who said that one day computers might replace humans.

02:52:18.280 --> 02:52:19.800
This seemed like a good idea.

02:52:20.370 --> 02:52:26.310
Henny's cat knew of several humans who needed replacing, like Farmer Giles and Constable Bulldog, for example.

02:52:26.310 --> 02:52:30.000
Oh, they'll never replace cats.

02:52:30.640 --> 02:52:33.800
because cats don't do anything useful

02:52:33.800 --> 02:52:37.670
and that's a great talent to have in the world today,

02:52:38.210 --> 02:52:39.120
