02:52:40.000 --> 02:52:41.320
It then occurred to him

02:52:41.320 --> 02:52:44.400
that a computer might be a very useful thing

02:52:44.400 --> 02:52:45.480
to have around the house,

02:52:45.890 --> 02:52:47.790
particularly for going out in rainy weather

02:52:47.790 --> 02:52:48.750
to buy cat food

02:52:48.750 --> 02:52:50.890
or for bringing him breakfast in bed

02:52:50.890 --> 02:52:52.550
or doing the housework.

02:52:53.590 --> 02:52:54.970
The more he thought about it,

02:52:55.120 --> 02:52:56.760
the more uses he could imagine.

02:52:57.010 --> 02:53:00.000
Oh, I wonder how much they cost.

02:53:00.350 --> 02:53:06.060
thought Henry's cat. Well, the obvious way to find out was to ask a computer, as they

02:53:06.060 --> 02:53:11.190
seemed to know everything, and there was one just near him answering questions. One man

02:53:11.190 --> 02:53:18.560
asked, "Oh, er, excuse me, how heavy is the world?" The computer did a lot of calculations

02:53:18.560 --> 02:53:25.730
and said, "Precisely, very heavy, two fifty decimal points."

02:53:25.730 --> 02:53:30.000
A little girl asked what dinner sauce ate for breakfast, but before the

02:53:30.060 --> 02:53:34.200
