02:56:23.030 --> 02:56:25.830
Oh, we could raffle the computer.

02:56:26.730 --> 02:56:29.480
That would be a good thing to win, wouldn't it?

02:56:30.000 --> 02:56:38.680
Ted Tortoise. "That's a silly idea. We'd have to buy it back again, wouldn't we?" said

02:56:38.680 --> 02:56:45.910
Mosey Mouse. "Oh, I was only trying to help," said Ted Tortoise, who went back into his

02:56:45.910 --> 02:56:55.570
shell and went to sleep. "It was a prize!" It was a silly idea, as they didn't own Pooter

02:56:55.570 --> 02:56:59.890
to give him away, even to themselves. Then a little voice said,

02:57:00.730 --> 02:57:06.740
an idea?" It was Sammy Snail, and as he didn't often get ideas, they all listened

02:57:06.740 --> 02:57:15.650
quietly. "Oh, what's your idea then?" said Henry's cat. "The computer is so clever, why

02:57:15.650 --> 02:57:24.330
don't you ask it how to pay for itself?" That did seem a very good idea. "Oh, why

02:57:24.330 --> 02:57:30.000
didn't you think of that?" said Henry's cat to Pooter. "You've never asked me

02:57:30.860 --> 02:57:44.310
With that, Pooter gave a sulky buzz and his lights went out.

02:57:44.310 --> 02:57:53.780
I'm sorry, Pooter. Will you please help us so that we can buy you?

02:57:53.780 --> 02:58:00.000
Pooter's eyes lit up and he started to click and buzz loudly. Everyone could see

02:58:00.000 --> 02:58:06.810
the pooter was sinking very high. He gave a happy bleep and said, "As you put the deposit on me

02:58:06.810 --> 02:58:14.260
with cat food and old clothes, you can start a barter club and charge two pence an item.

02:58:14.260 --> 02:58:21.390
I can sort out the things so everyone can swap their old rubbish for new rubbish."

02:58:21.390 --> 02:58:30.000
"Why do people want rubbish?" said Denise Duck. "That's a philosophical question.

02:58:34.570 --> 02:58:41.900
said Pooter. Chris Rabbit said, "That's a good idea. We put up notices everywhere saying,

02:58:41.900 --> 02:58:48.760
"Rabbit's exchange at two pence a time. See Henry's cat." Soon there were notices up everywhere.

02:58:48.760 --> 02:58:53.990
It wasn't long before they started to get results. The first person to come was Captain McGregor.

02:58:53.990 --> 02:59:00.000
He had a wooden right leg, so had lots of right shoes he didn't want, and he needed a raincoat for his

02:59:00.160 --> 02:59:08.270
So he gave Henry's cat two pence and said he'd be in touch as soon as someone with a parrot's raincoat requested some riot-footed shoes.

02:59:08.270 --> 02:59:16.830
The next person was a little boy. He gave some fireworks, only used once, for an Indian suit, when one was available.

02:59:16.830 --> 02:59:20.920
Then a lady came along with lots of household things for cooking and cleaning.

02:59:20.920 --> 02:59:25.810
She wanted to exchange these for a ticket to somewhere as far away as possible.

02:59:25.810 --> 02:59:30.000
After that, a little girl wanted to exchange her little brother for a ticket.

02:59:30.000 --> 02:59:34.270
for a racing car, but said if Henry's cat didn't have a car, he could have a brother

02:59:34.270 --> 02:59:39.540
anyway. Henry's cat was very pleased with the way things were going, and he patted Pooter

02:59:39.540 --> 02:59:45.170
on the head and tickled his switch. By the end of the day, Henry's cat had made over

02:59:45.170 --> 02:59:51.220
six pounds, but had a room full of rubbish. Henry's cat looked around at all the rubbish

02:59:51.220 --> 02:59:55.160
that had come in, and wondered how long it would be before he found the right things

02:59:55.160 --> 03:00:00.000
to exchange, so that the rubbish went out again. Well, we seem to

03:00:00.000 --> 03:00:06.570
getting a lot in, but when do you think it will start going out, Pooter?" Henry's cat inquired.

03:00:06.570 --> 03:00:22.170
Pooter clicked and hummed and flashed and said, "Three weeks, 2.791 days, by which time you will have earned 138 pounds and 64 pence."

03:00:22.170 --> 03:00:30.000
Well, even Henry's cat could work out that he could afford Pooter, and have enough over to buy lots of cat food, ice creams, and

03:00:30.090 --> 03:00:36.290
as well. It seemed a very good idea of Pootah's. Henry's cat then had another

03:00:36.290 --> 03:00:41.670
thought. "Oh, that sounds good, but how much rubbish will we have before we start

03:00:41.670 --> 03:00:54.610
exchanging it?" Pootah clicked and buzzed again and said, "Enough to fill four houses, two gardens, a woodshed, three wheelbarrows and a jam jar."

03:00:54.610 --> 03:01:00.000
Henry's cat thought it was time to go for a cup of tea if he could only get his foot out of a bicycle wheel.

03:01:00.090 --> 03:01:02.790
He had exchanged for six matching hot water bottles.

03:01:03.360 --> 03:01:07.260
"Al, you didn't tell me how much space we'd need, did you?"

03:01:07.580 --> 03:01:09.960
Said Henry's cat, a little bit peeved.

03:01:10.400 --> 03:01:13.290
"You didn't ask me, did you?"

03:01:13.640 --> 03:01:16.170
Said the computer, obviously a bit upset.

03:01:16.580 --> 03:01:18.880
"You're just like people.

03:01:19.930 --> 03:01:21.930
You ask silly questions

03:01:22.130 --> 03:01:26.630
and expect computers to come up with sensible answers.

03:01:27.140 --> 03:01:30.000
You only ask me how to make money.

03:01:30.600 --> 03:01:37.920
"You've already made six pounds, very good for the first time."

03:01:37.920 --> 03:01:43.590
Henry's cat realised he was really to blame, and he gave Pooter some oil and paper for supper,

03:01:43.590 --> 03:01:47.160
and turned him off so that he could have a rest.

03:01:47.160 --> 03:01:50.870
Then he went to sleep himself, which he'd just managed to do once he'd found his bed

03:01:50.870 --> 03:01:55.400
under all the rubbish.

03:01:55.400 --> 03:02:00.000
When Henry's cat awoke the next morning, he thought he was having a bad dream, and the

03:02:00.000 --> 03:02:01.920
and soon wake up for a nice breakfast.

03:02:01.920 --> 03:02:04.110
But then he realized it was not a dream

03:02:04.110 --> 03:02:07.040
and at any moment more rubbish would be arriving.

03:02:07.040 --> 03:02:10.340
Henry's cat made his way through the rubbish to the kitchen.

03:02:10.340 --> 03:02:12.650
Pooter had already switched himself on,

03:02:12.650 --> 03:02:14.650
was having oil and paper for breakfast.

03:02:14.650 --> 03:02:16.910
Henry's cat said,

03:02:16.910 --> 03:02:20.910
"Oh, I think you've been very clever getting all this rubbish,

03:02:20.910 --> 03:02:25.370
but now I wish I could get rid of it all."

03:02:25.370 --> 03:02:30.000
"That's easy. All you do is to get one of your friends."

03:02:30.890 --> 03:02:38.820
council is disfiguring the landscape, and they will take him away, and you as well.

03:02:40.130 --> 03:02:44.150
Oh, me as well? Why will they take me away?

03:02:45.290 --> 03:02:49.610
For causing a disfigurement to the landscape, said Pooter.

03:02:51.080 --> 03:02:54.400
Oh, but that's not very nice for me, is it?

03:02:54.400 --> 03:02:56.950
And he imagined himself being taken away.

03:02:57.740 --> 03:03:00.000
Well, you only asked me how.

03:03:00.000 --> 03:03:01.320
to get rid of the rubbish.

03:03:01.840 --> 03:03:05.120
You're not very easy to please, are you?

03:03:06.140 --> 03:03:07.840
Henry's cat had a vague idea.

03:03:08.120 --> 03:03:10.140
He'd have to solve this problem himself.

03:03:10.370 --> 03:03:12.290
So he went off to meet his friends.

03:03:13.410 --> 03:03:15.550
Chris Rabbit suggested wrapping all the rubbish up

03:03:15.550 --> 03:03:17.450
and making them presents into a lucky dip.

03:03:17.760 --> 03:03:20.220
But Henry's cat pointed out that this would be difficult

03:03:20.220 --> 03:03:23.180
with things like steam rollers and grandfather clocks.

03:03:23.840 --> 03:03:25.320
Denise Duck suggested a raffle,

03:03:25.640 --> 03:03:27.390
but Sammy Snell had a better idea.

03:03:27.730 --> 03:03:30.000
He suggested that they give all the rubbish to charity.

03:03:30.000 --> 03:03:35.950
as lots of people did that, and also give all the money they earned with the names of the people who gave it.

03:03:35.950 --> 03:03:40.280
People like to have their names on a list like that. It was a good idea.

03:03:40.280 --> 03:03:44.550
They all marched down to the town hall to see the mayor, and Henry's cat said,

03:03:44.550 --> 03:03:52.470
"Oh, dear sir or madam, we have collected many items of great value, which we are donating to charity,

03:03:52.470 --> 03:03:59.320
and have collected over £6 in genuine money for a good cause, such as removing all the rubbish we have."

03:04:01.210 --> 03:04:08.190
They were so impressed, he stood on a dustbin and made a speech, thanking everyone for donating their junk to charity.

03:04:08.190 --> 03:04:16.290
He gave a special thank you to Pooter, whose idea it was, and said the Council needed someone like Pooter to help on Council work.

03:04:16.290 --> 03:04:24.000
Henry's cat saw his opportunity and said to the Mayor, "Oh, as a matter of fact, Pooter is looking for a job.

03:04:24.000 --> 03:04:29.700
He only needs oil and paper for breakfast and a new plug every birthday."

03:04:30.220 --> 03:04:34.420
Mayor said Pooter could start work straight away. Well Pooter was very

03:04:34.420 --> 03:04:39.330
pleased with that and buzzed and flickered happily. Henry's cat waved goodbye to

03:04:39.330 --> 03:04:44.350
Pooter. He had decided he didn't need a computer to solve his problems and he

03:04:44.350 --> 03:04:49.410
certainly didn't need one to give him problems. He summed it all up by saying,

03:04:49.410 --> 03:04:57.650
"Oh computers are all right in their place but you can't count on them."

03:05:30.830 --> 03:05:31.540
Oh, oh, oh.

03:06:02.270 --> 03:06:02.760
It's true.

03:06:47.440 --> 03:07:00.000
is a trick. When Whizzer was up to his tricks, it meant trouble for everyone. First, he

03:07:00.000 --> 03:07:04.520
He teased Macduff and made him drop his rubber bone.

03:07:04.520 --> 03:07:09.920
Then he peddled round and round little Bun's hole until she wouldn't come out.

03:07:09.920 --> 03:07:15.740
As for Munch, he just hid in his shell until Whizzer went away.

03:07:15.740 --> 03:07:18.860
But worst of all was how Whizzer teased poor Bump.

03:07:18.860 --> 03:07:25.460
He went this way and that, yet wherever Bump stepped, there was naughty Whizzer.

03:07:25.460 --> 03:07:28.440
"Oh, Whizzer, you are a pest," said Bump.

03:07:30.730 --> 03:07:32.390
toppled against the squirrel's tree.

03:07:33.490 --> 03:07:35.230
Look what Whizzer made me do.

03:07:35.560 --> 03:07:36.960
Never mind, whistled Birdie.

03:07:37.680 --> 03:07:40.200
It wasn't your fault, called Mrs. Squirrel.

03:07:40.500 --> 03:07:42.240
Something should be done about that mouse.

03:07:42.420 --> 03:07:44.100
We'll soon have no acorns left.

03:07:44.610 --> 03:07:45.450
